  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Resilience and Adaptation for Water (CaRe4Water) - Turkwel</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Turkwel River basin within Turkana County is in the ASAL region of north-western Kenya. The main source of water for various uses comes from underground sources. Groundwater recharge in the county comes primarily from precipitation and surface water flows that infiltrate into the soil and replenish the aquifers. The main groundwater body in the basin is the Turkwel aquifer, which is the most important aquifer for water supply, particularly for irrigation and domestic use. The proposed project focuses on conducting a study on Managed Aquifer Recharge that is a water management method of refreshing groundwater stock in areas where a number of boreholes have been developed.</narrative>
  </description>
